From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yugidraft <yugidraft@localhost>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 20:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] core: return a temporarily banished card after its banisher effect is gone

A card banished "until" a later phase returns through MoveToField with
ret = 1, which compares the owner of the effect that banished it with the
owner of the returning effect. Time Chain (100463005) banishes with its
EVENT_BATTLED effect, which resets at the end of the Damage Phase, long before
the return. delete_effect then clears current.reason_effect (patch 0001), and
the compare read a null effect (UBSan in the nightly fuzz, n2 and n3 seed 73).

A missing effect cannot name another source, so the owner check now applies
only while both effects exist. The card returns as its text says. Cards whose
banisher effect is still alive keep the stock check.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
diff --git a/operations.cpp b/operations.cpp
--- a/operations.cpp
+++ b/operations.cpp
@@ -5736,3 +5736,6 @@ bool field::process(Processors::MoveToField& arg) {
 			return TRUE;
-		if((ret == 1) && (!(target->current.reason & REASON_TEMPORARY) || (target->current.reason_effect->owner != core.reason_effect->owner)))
+		// The effect that banished the card can be gone before the return (a Duel.RegisterEffect effect with a short reset,
+		// like Time Chain's EVENT_BATTLED effect); delete_effect then clears current.reason_effect. A missing effect cannot
+		// name another source, so the owner check only applies while both effects exist.
+		if((ret == 1) && (!(target->current.reason & REASON_TEMPORARY) || (target->current.reason_effect && core.reason_effect && target->current.reason_effect->owner != core.reason_effect->owner)))
 			return TRUE;
